IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `npa-types`

-- Notaries Public Act 1959 (Singapore) — ss 1-8, the whole Act.
--
-- Source: ../source/NPA1959.txt lines 47-147 (SSO PDF, current version as at
-- 05 Oct 2026, 2020 Revised Edition). The Act was last amended by Act 20 of
-- 2007, in force 1 June 2007 (Legislative History). Earlier texts were not
-- supplied, so every rule that is about a day refuses for a day before
-- 1 June 2007 rather than let today's text answer for it.

§ `Notaries Public Act 1959`

§§ `The period this encoding states the law for`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no source is encoded for a date before 1 June 2007` MEANS
    REFUSE "no source is encoded for a date before 1 June 2007: this encoding states the Notaries Public Act 1959 as last amended by Act 20 of 2007"

GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the law is encoded for` d MEANS
    IF d AT LEAST YMD 2007 6 1 THEN TRUE ELSE `no source is encoded for a date before 1 June 2007`

§§ `Long title, and 1. Short title`

-- INERT. "An Act relating to notaries public." [18 March 1965]
GIVETH A STRING
`s 1 — short title` MEANS "This Act is the Notaries Public Act 1959."

§§ `3. Appointment of notaries public`

-- s 3(2): "No person shall be appointed as a notary public unless he is a
-- practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore and has so practised for
-- not less than 7 years."
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 3(2)
GIVEN l IS A Lawyer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `qualified under s 3(2):` l IF
        l's `a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
    AND "not less than 7 years" ... l's `years practised as an advocate and solicitor in Singapore` AT LEAST 7

-- s 3(1): "The Senate may, from time to time, appoint fit and proper persons
-- to be notaries public for a period not exceeding 12 months."
-- s 3(3): "The Senate shall not make any appointment under this section
-- without consulting the Council of the Law Society of Singapore".
-- s 3(4): the Senate "shall have regard to the number of notaries public
-- already practising in the place where the applicant proposes to practise
-- and to the convenience of the inhabitants of that place, but, subject to
-- this, the Senate shall have absolute discretion in making or refusing to
-- make any such appointment and there shall be no appeal from its decision."
-- The s 3(4) considerations are the Senate's to weigh: the outcome says only
-- whether it MAY appoint.
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 3(1)-(4)
GIVEN l      IS A Lawyer
      months IS A NUMBER
      `the Council has been consulted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Appointment decision`
`the s 3(1) decision on` l `for` months `months, the Council consulted:` `the Council has been consulted` MEANS
    IF   null `reasons`
    THEN `the Senate may appoint, in its absolute discretion, and there is no appeal`
    ELSE `the Senate may not appoint` `reasons`
    WHERE
        `if not` holds label MEANS IF holds THEN EMPTY ELSE LIST label
        `reasons` MEANS
            concat (LIST
                (`if not` (l's `found by the Senate to be fit and proper`) "s 3(1): not a fit and proper person")
              , (`if not` (months AT MOST 12) "s 3(1): a period exceeding 12 months")
              , (`if not` (l's `a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`) "s 3(2): not a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore")
              , (`if not` (l's `years practised as an advocate and solicitor in Singapore` AT LEAST 7) "s 3(2): has practised for less than 7 years")
              , (`if not` `the Council has been consulted` "s 3(3): the Council of the Law Society has not been consulted"))

-- s 3(5): "If it appears to the Senate that any notary public is about to be
-- absent from Singapore for a period exceeding one month, the Senate may
-- appoint any person, being a practising advocate and solicitor in
-- Singapore, to be a notary public temporarily during the absence". The
-- 7-year rule of s 3(2) is not repeated here.
--
-- FORK F1: "a period exceeding one month" is a month by the calendar: an
-- absence from 1 March returning on 1 April is one month, and only a later
-- return exceeds it.
-- s 3(3) reaches this too: "The Senate shall not make any appointment under
-- this section without consulting the Council of the Law Society". (The first
-- version of this rule omitted it; the independent test pass found the gap.)
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 3(3), (5)
GIVEN l         IS A Lawyer
      leaves    IS A DATE
      returns   IS A DATE
      consulted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate may temporarily appoint` l `for an absence from` leaves `to` returns `, the Council consulted:` consulted IF
        `the law is encoded for` leaves
    AND "for a period exceeding one month" ... returns GREATER THAN `add months` leaves 1
    AND "being a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore" ... l's `a practising advocate and solicitor in Singapore`
    AND "s 3(3)" ... consulted

-- When an appointment has effect.
-- s 3(1): "for a period not exceeding 12 months".
-- s 3(6): "No temporary appointment ... shall have effect for a period longer
-- than 12 months and any such appointment shall lapse on the death or on the
-- return to Singapore of the notary public on account of whose departure from
-- Singapore the appointment was made."
-- s 5 and s 6: revocation ends it.
--
-- FORK F2: a period of n months from the day it takes effect runs to the day
-- before the same date n months on.
-- FORK F3: s 2 excludes from "notary public" a person whose appointment was
-- revoked "under section 5" and says nothing of s 6. A revocation under s 6
-- is read as ending the appointment all the same — "revoke the appointment"
-- has no other meaning.
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 ss 2, 3(1), 3(6), 5, 6
GIVEN a IS AN Appointment
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appointment` a `has effect on` d IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND d AT LEAST a's `takes effect on`
    AND d LESS THAN `add months` (a's `takes effect on`) `the months it can run`
    AND `not ended by` (a's `revoked under s 5 on`)
    AND `not ended by` (a's `revoked under s 6 on`)
    AND `not lapsed under s 3(6)`
    WHERE
        `the months it can run` MEANS
            IF a's `period in months` AT MOST 12 THEN a's `period in months` ELSE 12
        `not ended by` m MEANS
            CONSIDER m
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST e  THEN d LESS THAN e
        `not lapsed under s 3(6)` MEANS
            CONSIDER a's `kind`
            WHEN `an appointment under s 3(1)` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a temporary appointment under s 3(5)` who THEN
                    `not ended by` (a's `the absent notary returned on`)
                AND `not ended by` (a's `the absent notary died on`)

§§ `2. Interpretation`

-- s 2: "'notary public' means a person who has been appointed as a notary
-- public under section 3 but does not include any person whose appointment
-- has been revoked under section 5". "Senate" is the Senate of the Singapore
-- Academy of Law.
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 2
GIVEN name         IS A STRING
      appointments IS A LIST OF Appointment
      d            IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a notary public:` name `, by the appointments` appointments `, on` d IF
    any (GIVEN a YIELD a's `appointee` EQUALS name AND `the appointment` a `has effect on` d) appointments

-- s 3(7): "Every appointment under subsection (1) or subsection (5) and the
-- lapse of every temporary appointment under subsection (6) shall be
-- published in the Gazette." A duty with no time fixed; whether it was done
-- is an input on the appointment.

§§ `4. Privileges of notaries public`

-- s 4(1): every notary public "shall have and may exercise within Singapore
-- all the powers and functions which are ordinarily exercised by notaries
-- public in England." What those are is not in this source.
-- s 4(2): "Except for the purposes of and to the extent necessary to give
-- effect to subsection (3), powers under subsection (1) shall not include
-- power to administer any oath or affirmation in connection with any
-- affidavit or statutory declaration which is executed for the purpose of
-- being used in any court or place within Singapore or to take or attest any
-- such affidavit or statutory declaration."
-- s 4(3): "(a) administer any oath or affirmation in connection with any
-- affidavit or statutory declaration which is executed — (i) for the purpose
-- of confirming or proving the due execution of any document; (ii) by any
-- master or member of the crew of any vessel in respect of any matter
-- concerning the vessel; or (iii) for the purpose of being used in any court
-- or place outside Singapore; (b) take or attest any [such] affidavit or
-- statutory declaration ...; and (c) have and exercise such other powers and
-- functions as may be prescribed."
--
-- An affidavit that is neither for use in Singapore nor within (3)(a) turns
-- on the powers of notaries in England (s 4(1)) or on rules under s 8, and
-- neither source is here: that is a refusal, not a "no".
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 4(1)-(3)
GIVEN aff IS AN Affidavit
GIVETH AN `Oath power`
`the s 4 answer for` aff MEANS
    BRANCH IF aff's `purpose` EQUALS `confirming or proving the due execution of a document`
              THEN `the notary may administer the oath, and take or attest the document` "s 4(3)(a)(i), (b)"
           IF aff's `purpose` EQUALS `executed by the master or a crew member of a vessel about the vessel`
              THEN `the notary may administer the oath, and take or attest the document` "s 4(3)(a)(ii), (b)"
           IF aff's `to be used in a court or place outside Singapore`
              THEN `the notary may administer the oath, and take or attest the document` "s 4(3)(a)(iii), (b)"
           IF aff's `to be used in a court or place within Singapore`
              THEN `the notary may not, under s 4(2)`
           OTHERWISE REFUSE "this turns on the powers of notaries public in England (s 4(1)) or on rules under s 4(3)(c) and s 8, which this encoding does not have"

§§ `5. Misconduct of notaries public`

-- s 5: "If it appears to the Senate that any person being a notary public —
-- (a) has become a bankrupt or has made an arrangement with his creditors;
-- (b) has been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors of Singapore;
-- or (c) has been found to be guilty of such professional or other
-- misconduct as, in the opinion of the Senate, renders him unfit to practise
-- as a notary public, the Senate shall by order revoke the appointment of the
-- person and shall cause the order to be published in the Gazette."
-- A duty ("shall"), not a discretion.
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 5
GIVEN f IS A `Section 5 findings`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate must revoke the appointment, on` f IF
        "(a)" ... f's `has become a bankrupt or made an arrangement with creditors`
    ..  "(b)" ... f's `has been struck off the roll of advocates and solicitors`
    OR  "(c)" ... f's `guilty of misconduct the Senate thinks renders the person unfit to practise as a notary`

§§ `6. Revocation of appointment of notary public under special circumstances`

-- s 6: "The Senate may, by notification in the Gazette, revoke the
-- appointment of a notary public if the notary public requests that his
-- appointment be revoked." A power, opened only by the notary's request.
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 6
GIVEN `the notary has requested revocation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Senate may revoke under s 6, the notary having requested it:` `the notary has requested revocation` IF
    `the notary has requested revocation`

§§ `7. Penalty for exercise of functions of notary public by unauthorised persons`

-- s 7: "Any person who exercises within Singapore any of the functions of a
-- notary public otherwise than in accordance with the provisions of this Act
-- shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction before a
-- District Judge to a fine not exceeding $10,000." [20/2007]
-- Two ways of acting "otherwise than in accordance with" the Act are
-- encoded: not being a notary public that day, and acting beyond s 4.
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 7
GIVEN name               IS A STRING
      appointments       IS A LIST OF Appointment
      d                  IS A DATE
      `exercised a notarial function within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the function was within the s 4 powers`         IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 is contravened by` name `, by the appointments` appointments `, on` d `, having` `exercised a notarial function within Singapore` `, within powers:` `the function was within the s 4 powers` IF
        `the law is encoded for` d
    AND `exercised a notarial function within Singapore`
    AND NOT (    `a notary public:` name `, by the appointments` appointments `, on` d
             AND `the function was within the s 4 powers`)

@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 7
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7 — maximum fine` MEANS 10000

@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 7
GIVETH A STRING
`s 7 — the court` MEANS "on conviction before a District Judge"

§§ `8. Rules`

-- s 8(1): "The Chief Justice, after consultation with the Senate, may make
-- rules — (a) for the guidance and control of persons entitled to exercise
-- the functions of a notary public under this Act; (b) to fix the fees
-- payable to notaries public; (c) to fix the fees payable to the Singapore
-- Academy of Law by any person on appointment as a notary public, and on
-- renewal of such appointment; and (d) prescribing the powers and functions
-- of notaries public."
-- s 8(2): "All rules made under this section shall be published in the
-- Gazette, and shall come into force on the date of such publication or on
-- such later date as may be specified in the rules."
@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 8
GIVEN r IS A Rules
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `made within s 8(1):` r IF
        r's `made by the Chief Justice`
    AND "after consultation with the Senate" ... r's `after consulting the Senate`

@ref Notaries Public Act 1959 s 8(2)
GIVEN r IS A Rules
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the day s 8(2) brings into force` r MEANS
    CONSIDER r's `published in the Gazette on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING                  -- not published: not in force
    WHEN JUST p  THEN CONSIDER r's `later commencement date specified`
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST p
                      WHEN JUST l  THEN IF l GREATER THAN p THEN JUST l ELSE JUST p
